This is much better. I can see the direction now, and I think you're building something that's going to be easy to maintain.

I have one recommendation before we continue:

**Don't use full URLs for your own pages.**

Instead of:

```html
<a href="https://luckypikas.github.io/loveqna/about.html">About LoveQnA</a>
```

use

```html
<a href="about.html">About LoveQnA</a>
```

Instead of

```html
<a href="https://luckypikas.github.io/loveqna/dictionary.html">Dictionary</a>
```

use

```html
<a href="dictionary.html">Dictionary</a>
```

Instead of

```html
<a href="https://luckypikas.github.io/loveqna/resources.html">Resources</a>
```

use

```html
<a href="resources.html">Resources</a>
```

### Why?

If you ever move the website, rename the repository, or test locally on your computer, **every link will still work**. This is standard practice for static websites.

Only use full URLs for sites that are **outside** your LoveQnA website, such as:

* YouTube
* Poe
* Substack
* GitHub Wiki

