# I also have a suggestion about your wording.

I think this sentence is excellent:

> **We don't give dating advice. We conduct behavioral investigations.**

I would keep it exactly as the opening statement.

But I'd make one small change later.

Instead of saying

> We conduct behavioral investigations.

I'd say

> **We investigate relationship behavior.**

or

> **We investigate relationship patterns, human behavior, and decision-making.**

Why?

Because "behavioral investigations" sounds almost like a police department or private investigator. Your site is broader than that. You're investigating stories, psychology, communication, scams, decision-making, compatibility, leadership, trust, and human behavior.

